---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = 'Can You Use Foreign Credit Cards in China? A Realistic Look';
const description = 'Where Visa and Mastercard actually work in China, ATM withdrawal costs, and why mobile payments are the way to go for travelers in 2026.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} lang="en">
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-8 not-prose">
      <a href="/en/payment/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-gray-400 hover:text-gray-700 transition no-underline group">
        <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 transition-transform group-hover:-translate-x-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"/>
        </svg>
        Back to Payment
      </a>
    </nav>
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="mb-12">
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-3">💳 Payment</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4 leading-tight">
        Can You Use Foreign Credit Cards in China?
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-6">A realistic look at where your Visa or Mastercard will work.</p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-gray-500">
        <span>📅 Last updated: June 2026</span>
        <span>⏱️ 4 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Quick Answer Box -->
    <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-50 to-amber-50 border-l-4 border-orange-500 rounded-r-2xl p-8 mb-12 not-prose">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-orange-900 mb-4">🎯 Quick Answer</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-orange-800 leading-relaxed">
        <strong>Don't rely on your physical credit card as your main payment method in China.</strong> Foreign Visa/Mastercard works at international hotels, luxury malls, and airports — but most daily places (restaurants, taxis, shops) won't accept it. Use Alipay or WeChat Pay instead.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Main Content -->
    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">
        Let me be direct with you: <strong>do not rely on your physical credit card as your main way to pay in China.</strong>
      </p>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">
        I'm not saying it won't work. It will — in some places. But China's payment ecosystem is built around QR codes and mobile apps, and your foreign-issued Visa or Mastercard is just not part of that system in the way you'd expect. Setting up <a href="/en/payment/setup-alipay/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">Alipay</a> or <a href="/en/payment/setup-wechat/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">WeChat Pay</a> is the smarter move.
      </p>

      <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">💳</span> Where Your Foreign Card Actually Works
      </h2>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">Here's the honest picture:</p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-8 not-prose">
        <div class="bg-green-50 border border-green-200 rounded-2xl p-5">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-green-800 uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">✅ Yes, works</h3>
          <ul class="text-sm text-green-700 space-y-1">
            <li>• International hotel chains (Hilton, Marriott, InterContinental)</li>
            <li>• High-end department stores and luxury malls</li>
            <li>• Major international airports</li>
            <li>• Some international restaurants</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-2xl p-5">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-red-800 uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">❌ Probably won't work</h3>
          <ul class="text-sm text-red-700 space-y-1">
            <li>• Neighborhood restaurants and street food stalls</li>
            <li>• Taxis and ride-hailing (Didi uses WeChat/Alipay only)</li>
            <li>• Local shops, convenience stores, supermarkets</li>
            <li>• Anywhere that only accepts UnionPay (most places)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">
        The frustrating part is that many Chinese merchants have POS machines, but those machines are configured for <strong>UnionPay</strong> — China's domestic card network. Your foreign Visa or Mastercard can't connect to the UnionPay network. So even when a terminal is sitting right there, your card might get declined.
      </p>

      <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">🏧</span> Using ATMs
      </h2>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">
        ATMs are a different story. Most ATMs at Bank of China, ICBC, and China Construction Bank accept foreign Visa and Mastercard for cash withdrawals. The fees aren't great (typically ¥15–30 per withdrawal plus your bank's foreign transaction fee), but it works when you need cash.
      </p>

      <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">💡</span> The Bottom Line
      </h2>

      <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-8 not-prose">
        <p class="text-gray-700">Bring your credit card as a backup, but set up mobile payments as your primary method. You'll have a much smoother trip.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Related Guides -->
    <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-8 not-prose mt-12">
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">📚 Related Guides</h3>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="/en/payment/payment-guide/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100">
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">How to Pay in China</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Complete payment overview</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/en/payment/setup-alipay/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100">
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">How to Set Up Alipay</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Step-by-step setup guide</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>